@startuml
title T12-WF13 — AI Renewal Management Agent (Sequence)
autonumber
participant "Schedule Trigger" as SCHED
participant "n8n WF13\nRenewal Management" as N8N
participant "NestJS Backend" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Gemini API" as AI
participant "Communication API" as COMM
participant "NestJS Review Module" as APPROVAL

SCHED -> N8N: Daily renewal scan
activate N8N
N8N -> API: GET contracts due in renewal window
API -> DB: Query eligible CustomerContract records
DB --> API: Contract IDs and renewal dates
API --> N8N: Due contracts
loop For each contract
N8N -> API: GET contract/customer/status details
API -> DB: Read contract and customer
DB --> API: Current status and source dates
API --> N8N: Contract context
N8N -> N8N: Calculate urgency from actual renewal dates
N8N -> AI: Draft renewal recommendation and message
AI --> N8N: Draft/recommendation
N8N -> N8N: Validate customer, contract and dates against source
N8N -> API: Save renewal draft only
API -> DB: Persist draft and source provenance
DB --> API: Draft ID
API --> N8N: Draft saved
alt Approved template + consent + policy permit automatic sending
N8N -> COMM: Request approved message send via NestJS
COMM -> COMM: Verify permissions, consent and idempotency
COMM --> N8N: Sent / failed result
else Human approval required or auto-send not allowed
N8N -> APPROVAL: Create/ensure one pending approval task
APPROVAL -> DB: Persist task idempotently with draft/contract reference
DB --> APPROVAL: Task ID (existing or newly created)
APPROVAL --> N8N: Pending approval; no message sent
end
N8N -> API: Record RenewalAttempt status
API -> DB: Persist attempt/status idempotently
DB --> API: Attempt ID
API --> N8N: Attempt recorded
end
deactivate N8N
note over N8N,COMM
n8n does not send SMTP directly. NestJS owns contract data, renewal state, approval/consent policy and communication delivery; the scheduled workflow calls the canonical APIs.
end note

note over APPROVAL,DB
ReviewTask supports a non-Lead target through `target_entity_type` and `target_entity_id`. For renewal approval, set the target type to `CustomerContract` and the target ID to the contract UUID; NestJS validates the allowlisted type, record existence, authorization, policy, idempotency and audit.
end note
@enduml
